scope='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Numerical scope | PhaseAtlas</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="project.css"><header><a class="brand" href="index.html">PhaseAtlas</a><nav><a href="studio.html">PDE Studio</a><a href="workbench.html">Workbench</a></nav></header><main><section class="section"><p class="eyebrow">NUMERICAL SCOPE / 18 OCTOBER 2026</p><h1>Make the model fit the method.</h1><div class="three"><article><h2>Periodic</h2><p>1D/2D rectangular periodic domains. Fourier derivatives and ETDRK4; supported constant diagonal linear operators with an explicit remainder.</p></article><article><h2>Second-order bounded</h2><p>1D/2D rectangles. Constant nonnegative diagonal diffusion; Dirichlet, Neumann and passive Robin data. Robin coefficients are nonnegative constants or parameters, not both zero.</p></article><article><h2>Fourth-order bounded</h2><p>1D intervals. Negative constant leading fourth-order term per field and two admissible linear boundary rows at each end. No 2D nonperiodic fourth-order backend.</p></article></div><h2>Shared limits</h2><p>One to three fields. CPU Float64 arithmetic. Explicit nonlinear terms still require time-step checks. Centered transport is not a shock-capturing scheme. The interface rejects unsupported expressions, but cannot certify continuum well-posedness of every accepted model.</p><h2>Interpretation</h2><p>Three-level comparisons estimate observed behavior. Balance closure and boundary residuals test discrete consistency. Finite-time parameter scans do not trace solution branches. Imported data and supplied reference formulas remain subject to verification.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="submission-2026/PhaseAtlas_Article.html">Methods and executed results</a><a class="button" href="downloads/CUSTOM_PDE_STUDIO.md">Detailed numerical documentation</a></div></section></main></html>'''
